THOUGHT: NullAway complains that the enhanced-for expression `joinOn` is @Nullable. Even though the code sets `joinOn` to `Collections.emptyList()` when null, the cast from `task.getInputData().get("joinOn")` is from a `Map<String, Object>` and NullAway likely infers it as `@Nullable List<String>`. A simple fix is to avoid a nullable variable by initializing `joinOn` to an empty list and only reassigning it when the map value is non-null. I’ll update the code accordingly and then run the compile task to confirm the error count drops by one and no new errors are introduced.

```bash
cd /home/vscode/nullness-benchmarks/conductor && sed -i '50,53c\        List<String> joinOn = Collections.emptyList();
        Object joinOnObj = task.getInputData().get("joinOn");
        if (joinOnObj instanceof List) {
            //noinspection unchecked
            joinOn = (List<String>) joinOnObj;
        }' core/src/main/java/com/netflix/conductor/core/execution/tasks/ExclusiveJoin.java && ./gradlew conductor-core:compileJava -x test -q > new_build_output.log 2>&1 && grep -n "DEREFERENCE_NULLABLE" new_build_output.log || true
```

